        <mxCell id="notes_box" value="Notes &amp; assumptions" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fafafa;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontStyle=1;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="640" width="1260" height="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Hard rule — never daisy-chain power strips.&lt;/b&gt;  Every extension cord and every power strip plugs DIRECTLY into a wall outlet. Each station uses the closest outlet in proximity.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;1. Mains capacity:&lt;/b&gt; verified — we have set up in this room before with this same load profile, no breaker issues.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;2. Outlet-to-strip mapping:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;     • Left-wall outlet  →  Pi Rack  +  VHF Station   (short runs; built-in strip cords sufficient)&#10;     • Right-wall outlet  →  Station 2   (top-wall run; uses the &lt;b&gt;50 ft&lt;/b&gt; extension)&#10;     • Bottom-wall outlet  →  Station 1 (uses the &lt;b&gt;25 ft&lt;/b&gt; extension)  +  Station 3 (short run; built-in strip cord)&#10;     &lt;i&gt;Confirm: is Station 1 actually closer to the bottom outlet, or to the left-wall outlet?&lt;/i&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;3. UPS coverage:&lt;/b&gt; only the Pi 400 is behind the UPS. WiFi AP plugs into the rack's strip directly. &lt;i&gt;(Confirm — should UPS cover the AP as well?)&lt;/i&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;4. WinKey Mini:&lt;/b&gt; USB-powered from the laptop; not counted on Station 3's strip.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;5. Talk-In Station:&lt;/b&gt; not on this diagram — whoever brings the rig owns its own power, and it doesn't draw from any of the four station strips." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="680" width="1240" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
